course: dictionary
lesson: 11338
title: Zakat: sharing wealth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Zakat is a word from Islam, and you can also meet it in maths. You can work out much of its meaning from the words around it. «The Five Pillars are: the declaration of faith, prayer five times a day, giving to the poor (zakat), fasting in Ramadan and the pilgrimage to Mecca (Hajj).» The brackets show that zakat is one of the Five Pillars, so it is something important that people do, not a food or a place.
explain: Zakat is a noun, and you may also see it spelled zakah. It means giving a fixed part of your wealth each year to the poor and needy. Wealth means the money and things you own. «Many faiths and humanists teach that the rich should share with the poor; Christians give to charity, Muslims give zakat and Sikhs share food in the langar.» Here zakat is one way of sharing with the poor, like charity and the langar.
explain: In maths, zakat is a percentage problem. For most savings it is one-fortieth, which is 2.5 per cent. If 400 pounds has been kept for a full year above the set minimum, then 2.5% of 400 is 10 pounds. Check your answer by swapping in the meaning: is 10 pounds one-fortieth of 400 pounds? Yes, so it makes sense.
fact: Zakat means giving a fixed part of one's wealth each year to the poor and needy.
fact: Zakat is one of the Five Pillars of Islam.
fact: For most savings, zakat is one-fortieth, which is 2.5 per cent.
fact: 2.5% of 400 pounds is 10 pounds.
fact: Zakat al-fitr is a gift of food given before Eid.
exercise: «The Five Pillars are: ... giving to the poor (zakat) ...» In this sentence, what is zakat? | A holiday in Mecca | A type of prayer | *One of the Five Pillars, giving to the poor | A kind of food
exercise: For most savings, what fraction of wealth is zakat? | *One-fortieth | One-tenth | Half | One-hundredth
exercise: In maths, what is 2.5% of 400 pounds? | 4 pounds | *10 pounds | 25 pounds | 40 pounds
test: Who is zakat given to? | Animals | The rich | *The poor and needy | Only to the family of the giver
test: «Christians give to charity, Muslims give zakat and Sikhs share food in the langar.» Which faith is named as giving zakat? | Sikhs | Humanists | *Muslims | Christians
exam: Which phrase means a gift of food given before Eid? | Five Pillars | *zakat al-fitr | give zakat | pay zakat
